<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Justinian II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">669–<a href="/years/711">711</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Justinian Rhinotmetos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Justinian II was a Byzantine emperor of the Heraclian dynasty who reigned from 685 to 695 and again from 705 to 711. In 688 he agreed with the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Abd al-Malik to share the revenues of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, and he campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/struma">Strymon</a>, resettling many in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. Deposed and mutilated in 695, he regained the throne before being killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justinian-ii.jpg" alt="Justinian II" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marvelfannumber1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Justinian_ii_(2,_cropped_and_askew).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
